{"name":"Ivy Enchantment","hex":"#93a272","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ivy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several woody, climbing, or trailing evergreen plants of the genus Hedera.","Any similar plant of any genus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivy"},{"term":"enchantment","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of enchanting or the feeling of being enchanted.","Something that enchants; a magical spell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enchantment"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hedera","blocks":[{"text":"Hedera, commonly called ivy, is a genus of 12–15 species of evergreen climbing or ground-creeping woody plants in the family Araliaceae, native to Western Europe, Central Europe, Southern Europe, Macaronesia, northwestern Africa and across central-southern Asia east to Japan and Taiwan. Several species are cultivated as climbing ornamentals, and the name ivy especially denotes common ivy, known in North America as \"English ivy\", which is frequently planted to clothe brick walls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg/330px-Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedera","wikidata":"Q26771"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Ivy_fruits.JPG/500px-Ivy_fruits.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Ivy_fruits.JPG/1280px-Ivy_fruits.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Ivy_fruits.JPG/500px-Ivy_fruits.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hedera helix adult leaves and unripe berries in Ayrshire, Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F